---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import StaticPage from '@/components/ui/StaticPage.astro';

const title = 'About Glitch';
const description =
  'Glitch is a social platform for gamers: a catalogue of tens of thousands of games, community reviews, and a feed of what the people you follow are playing.';
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <StaticPage
    title="A social home for people who play games"
    intro="Glitch pairs a full game catalogue with the one thing store pages never have: what real people think, in public."
  >
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      Glitch is two things in one place. The first is a catalogue: tens of thousands of games,
      searchable and filterable by genre, platform, and release status. The second is a community.
      Every game has a page where people leave reviews and scores, and a feed that shows you what
      the players you follow are playing, reviewing, and rating.
    </p>
    <p>
      We pull game data from <a href="https://www.igdb.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IGDB</a>,
      the open game database, so the catalogue stays current without us copying it by hand. Reviews
      and scores come from Glitch users only: an external reference rating is shown beside ours so
      you can tell the two apart.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it came from</h2>
    <p>
      Glitch started as a personal project in August 2025, before the course it now serves as a
      final project had begun, as a way to learn how a real full-stack application fits together:
      server rendering, a typed API, a relational database, and a design system that holds up in
      both light and dark mode.
    </p>
    <p>
      It grew into a monorepo with a NestJS and Prisma backend, an Astro front end with React
      islands, PostgreSQL, Redis, and Docker images for development and production. The
      early commits are from that learning period; the architecture since then is the result of
      rebuilding the same idea properly.
    </p>

    <h2>What is built in</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A catalogue with search, filters, and per-game detail pages.</li>
      <li>Reviews with scores, likes, and comments.</li>
      <li>A social feed, profiles, and a follow graph.</li>
      <li>An admin panel for moderating reviews and users.</li>
      <li>Light and dark themes, both designed, not inverted.</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      Questions, bug reports, or feedback? Head to <a href="/support">Support</a>.
    </p>
  </StaticPage>
</MainLayout>
